WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:02.300
Hey Youtubers, it's Charlie.

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:05.500
Since there's a whole bunch of Suicide Squad stuff that's been happening lately,

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.080
I thought it was time for a bonus video.

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:11.040
You know, I think one thing is clear. Based on all the stuff that's coming from the set,

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:15.440
the people making this movie do not care how much we know about it going into it.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:18.720
Batman was just seen recently on set chasing the Joker around.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:25.420
And when I say Batman, I mean a person in a Batman costume - not Ben Affleck. He wasn't seen on set.

00:00:25.429 --> 00:00:29.429
It gives you the feeling that the story might be going to like an "Assault on Arkham" place.

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:34.280
Especially because of some of the images we saw of Will Smith as Deadshot with Harley Quinn on the set.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:39.640
Really what I think is going on is they're just blending a lot of elements from some really popular Suicide Squad stories.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:41.720
Batman: Assault on Arkham being one of them,

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:45.180
but, you know, I think they're weaving a lot of classic John Ostrander in there too.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:48.660
David Ayer's calling it the dirty dozen of the DC Universe.

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:51.940
But I'm also thinking of it as a little bit of a Raid: Redemption movie.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:54.700
If you haven't seen that movie, it's this really awesome Indonesian film.

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:59.174
It's basically Batman: Assault on Arkham with way more action, way less talking.

00:00:59.174 --> 00:01:03.954
If you've never seen Dirty Dozen, it's like this Charles Bronson World War II movie where, you know,

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:09.320
prior to D-Day this group of people has to come together, this group of convicts has to team up

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:13.640
to take down a bunch of high ranking Nazis in this "suicide mission"

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:19.600
That was from 1967. The version of Suicide Squad as we know it now, you know, created by John Ostrander

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:25.720
started in 1987 so you could say that he drew a lot of inspiration from The Dirty Dozen.

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:29.560
Because I haven't done a whole lot of Suicide Squad videos, just to get you guys pumped up for the movie,

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:33.400
to get you prepped, here are my top 5 stories that I think you should check out first.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:37.420
Starting with #5. Batman: Assault on Arkham - the animated movie.

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:42.180
This might be a Batman story, but really it's a Suicide Squad story with Batman in it.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:45.300
They just put Batman's name on the movie so that it would sell more copies.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:48.360
Most of the focus of the film is the Suicide Squad itself.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:52.900
Since it's an animated movie for a younger audience, you know, I think it has a lot of silly humor in it

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:55.280
that we won't see in the Suicide Squad movie.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:02:02.360
The tone of that will be closer to what Zack Snyder is going for in Batman v. Superman and the Justice League franchise that he's spinning out.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:06.480
There will be humor, I mean it'll still be a funny film.. but it'll be a little more tongue-in-cheek.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:08.760
On to #4. The Raid: Redemption.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:15.454
Basically like, the best example of what an action film should be, with like.. all the fat, all the excess boiled out.

00:02:15.454 --> 00:02:20.460
The really good thing about this film is that you've probably never heard of any of these actors before

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:23.598
so there's no weird meta-stuff going on that takes you out of the story.

00:02:23.598 --> 00:02:30.420
A SWAT team is trying to take down a drug lord who's on the top floor of a building that he's turned into his personal fortress.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:36.180
The challenges they face as they fight their way to the top floor, like on each of the floors, becomes progressively more difficult.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:38.340
The fighting style itself is pretty badass.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:41.180
Think of a cross between, like, classic John Woo..

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:44.680
and the kind of parkour stuff you saw in Captain America: Winter Soldier.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:48.866
The story is told from the perspective of a rookie character on his first day on the job.

00:02:48.866 --> 00:02:51.160
You don't even need the subtitles to enjoy it.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:56.240
It's just the perfect example of how you pace an action movie that's not trying to be another type of movie.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:00.760
It's not trying to be some gripping drama. It's a badass action film plain and simple.

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:06.020
On to #3. Batman: Mad Love. Basically the origin story of Harley Quinn.

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:10.440
So Mad Love is actually by Paul Dini and Bruce Timm, you know, two people..

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:11.980
from Batman: The Animated Series.

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:16.620
Which, you know, my personal favorite Batman TV show of all time. I don't know if it's ever gonna be topped.

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:22.860
They go deep on Harlene Quinzelle, you know, one time promising psychiatrist who just fell madly in love..

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:26.420
with her patient, and went on to become the Joker's greatest sidekick.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:31.920
It does a good job of having fun with that, while at the same time showing you how tragic her life has been.

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:36.000
And how she can totally step out from the Joker's shadow if given the opportunity.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.160
It's easy to understand how some people think that she's just a backup to the Joker, but..

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:42.741
in her own right, she's an amazing character.

00:03:42.741 --> 00:03:46.241
I feel like whenever Margo Robbie was cast as Harley Quinn,

00:03:46.241 --> 00:03:50.560
this is probably the story they gave her to read so that she could read about Harley's character.

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:54.620
On to #2. Basically all of Gail Simone's run on Secret Six.

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:59.200
That started with the Villains United story arc and went all the way up to the New 52.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:02.460
She really explored what's going on in Deadshot's headspace.

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:06.160
Will Smith - you know, probably gonna be the biggest star in Suicide Squad next to Ben Affleck.

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:11.820
If he truely is in the film, and it's not just a Batman suit cameo with someone else inside it.

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:14.944
I don't think the entire film is just going to focus on his character.

00:04:14.944 --> 00:04:19.060
But given that Tom Hardy dropped out, and the film was originally centered on Rick Flag..

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:20.820
they might have changed some things up.

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:26.100
And finally, my #1 prep story - Suicide Squad: From the Ashes, by John Ostrander himself.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:31.700
This is a story written by the Suicide Squad creator, like, the person who wrote the best Suicide Squad stories..

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:37.040
that invokes a lot of the classic Suicide Squad canon while telling a modern day story.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:40.060
It's really about all these bad characters, these Suicide Squad characters..

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:42.620
picking themselves up after getting their asses handed to them.

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:44.907
Amanda Waller had been kicked out of Checkmate,

00:04:44.907 --> 00:04:49.620
Rick Flag Jr. just barely survived this nuclear blast, almost got his face melted off..

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:55.600
So he uses this very "Arrow" type storytelling device where he flashes back to Rick Flag Jr.'s past.

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:59.360
So Ostrander uses Rick Flag to do the flashbacks in the present day

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:01.380
he's like the connective tissue, that character.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:04.020
But like I said, that was supposed to be Tom Hardy in the film..

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:08.620
he dropped out, was replaced by Joel Kinnaman who played Robocop, if you guys haven't seen that movie.

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:14.160
Will Smith was cast, so.. him being the bigger actor, I think that they might shift the film

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:17.920
and do flashbacks using Will Smith's character, using the Deadshot character.

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:21.000
We saw him on set in like.. pimp-alicious clothing, so:

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:26.040
either Deadshot just dresses like a pimp all the time, or he's going to be the connective tissue of the film.

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:30.120
Arguably that should be Harley Quinn's relationship with the Joker.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:33.000
Really I think the connective tissue in any Suicide Squad story

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:35.560
would be Harley Quinn's relationship with the Joker.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:39.100
Just, that's just way more interesting than any of the other Suicide Squad characters.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:43.620
I think a lot of that'll be in there because it seems like most of the film is going to be them chasing the Joker down.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:47.940
But you could look at the fact that Margot Robbie, playing Harley Quinn, and Will Smith..

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:51.420
just did a movie together called Focus where they did have a lot of chemistry together.

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:56.540
So you can see how they might use Deadshot in a Harley Quinn/Joker storyline within this movie.

00:05:56.540 --> 00:06:01.420
They kinda did that during Batman: Assault on Arkham which is why I keep going back to that story.

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:05.100
Part of me feels like a bunch of executives watched that animated film after it was done

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:09.460
and saw that people loved it so much, and they thought, "Hey, why don't we make a live-action version of this?"

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:11.160
Here's my big question for you though:

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:15.500
Given all the things we've seen from the set, which character are you most excited to see?

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:17.300
I mean, there are a lot of characters in the film.

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:21.980
As cool as Harley Quinn is, and as curious as I am about Jared Leto's Joker..

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:25.820
I am most excited to see Cara Delevingne's Enchantress.

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:29.040
Seriously, this movie isn't shying away from meta-humans.

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:32.620
We have Killer Croc.. as long as he doesn't look like one of the Koopas,

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:35.660
you know from the Super Mario Bros. old movie, I think we'll be fine.

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:37.980
King Shark is also gonna be a lot of fun too.

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:41.620
David Ayer keeps reiterating how much he wants to do this live-action.

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:46.220
They will need to use a little bit of CG touch-up, but most of this is actually going to be practical effects.

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:50.600
That's actually why we've gotten so many pictures of the Batman chasing Joker around on the street..

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:53.000
Because they're not filming it on a Green Screen Studio.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:55.520
So there's actually quite a bit to be excited about in this film.

00:06:55.520 --> 00:07:00.480
As cool as the action is and as much as I want them to do like - a DC, Raid: Redemption movie..

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:03.678
this film will be made or broken on the strength of its characters.

00:07:03.678 --> 00:07:06.660
I feel like they have enough diversity of really good actors

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:11.134
that the film won't live or die on the strength of Jared Leto's Joker performance.

00:07:11.134 --> 00:07:13.540
But, he is definitely a big part of the equation.

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:16.580
Every superhero film is only as great as its villain.

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:18.420
And in a film where the villains are the heroes,

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:21.674
Jared Leto's Joker is the closest thing we actually have to a villain.

00:07:21.674 --> 00:07:25.640
I suppose who you think the villain is depends on which character you identify with the most.

00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:29.980
Since it's Wednesday, my next video is gonna be my Top 10 Episodes from Arrow season 3.

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:33.060
So be sure to subscribe to get that, I should have that up by late tonight.

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:37.560
But if there's any Suicide Squad videos you guys want me to do next, just leave requests in the comments.

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:42.100
Just in case you guys haven't seen it yet, you can click here for my Top 10 episodes of The Flash this season.

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:47.525
And you can click here for my Flash season 2 promo video. There's like a small promo, and my predictions.

00:07:47.525 --> 00:07:50.580
Thank you so much for watching! Everybody, let's high-five, I'll see you guys tonight.

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:57.420
(music playing)

